<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Surveys' cross-section surface. The leaf existed as its own project because its only
    consumer outside the section sat in Base: SendSurveyReminderJob in
    Humans.Infrastructure/Jobs. **That is no longer true** — the job moved into
    Humans.Surveys/Contracts/ at G5 lane 5b-5 (nobodies-collective/Humans#866), and
    ISurveyReminderSender now has no consumer outside this section at all. Shell names only
    the job's concrete type, which is a Humans.Surveys type. Left standing deliberately:
    collapsing a leaf or shrinking interface surface is Peter's call, not a job move's side
    effect (lane 5b-1's open item 24 answered "leave" on the four in the same position).

    It holds exactly one interface. Nothing else Surveys exposes has a consumer outside
    the section — the three controllers, the DI registration and the section's own tests
    are the whole fan-in — so the rest stays internal. There is deliberately no
    ISurveyServiceRead here: the read interface shipped empty in v1 and no section ever
    consumed it (design §15 step 5, "keep an interface only where something needs the seam").

    References Humans.Interfaces only.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
